/T (This lab demonstrates fundamental relational database management using phpMyAdmin, a free web-based tool for MySQL and MariaDB that supports both graphical administration and direct SQL execution. Within the first_dbs database, an It_students table was constructed to store academic records including student names, CGPAs, departments, and university names. By executing the full workflow of table creation, data insertion, and record retrieval, the exercise establishes a strong practical understanding of structured data operations while laying essential groundwork for future topics in database security.)
/E (This lab demonstrates fundamental relational database management using phpMyAdmin, a free web-based tool for MySQL and MariaDB that supports both graphical administration and direct SQL execution. Within the first_dbs database, an It_students table was constructed to store academic records including student names, CGPAs, departments, and university names. By executing the full workflow of table creation, data insertion, and record retrieval, the exercise establishes a strong practical understanding of structured data operations while laying essential groundwork for future topics in database security.)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [10]
>>
endobj
