/P 286 0 R
/E (SQL commands are categorized according to their function: Data Definition Language \(DDL\) is responsible for creating, altering, and organizing the framework of a database, whereas Data Manipulation Language \(DML\) manages the records held within that framework by enabling users to insert, modify, remove, and query information. Through practical exercises with CREATE, INSERT, UPDATE, and SELECT statements, this lab strengthened your grasp of how to manage and retrieve data inside a MySQL database via phpMyAdmin.)
/Pg 22 0 R
/K [5]
>>
