535 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 290 0 R
/E (Relational databases depend on structured connections between distinct datasets to minimize redundancy and maintain data integrity. In SQL, a Foreign Key serves as the fundamental link between two tables by directly referencing the Primary Key of another table. Once these relationships are established, JOIN clauses are utilized to seamlessly query and merge records from multiple tables into a single comprehensive view. This practical exercise demonstrates these core relational concepts by connecting student academic profiles with their corresponding fee payment records, enabling targeted, cross-referenced data retrieval across both tables.)
/Pg 26 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
