/E (EXPLAIN SELECT * FROM students WHERE name LIKE 'S%';)
/Pg 35 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
625 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 299 0 R
/E (This query performs a prefix pattern match using the same idx_student_name index, resulting in an access type of range. Because of the trailing wildcard \('S%'\), MySQL cannot look up a single exact coordinate and instead finds the start of the "S" section and sweeps sequentially across a span of matching index entries. )
/Pg 35 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
626 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 299 0 R
/T (EXCERSICE 1)
/E (EXCERSICE 1)
/Pg 35 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
627 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 299 0 R
/E (EXPLAIN SELECT * FROM students WHERE name = 'Sara';)
/Pg 35 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
628 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 299 0 R
/E (This query performs an exact point-lookup using the idx_student_name index, resulting in an access type of ref. Because it searches for one specific string \('Sara'\), MySQL jumps directly to that exact coordinate in the index tree without scanning surrounding entries. )
/Pg 35 0 R
/K [10]
>>
endobj
